{
 "_note": "Group-level topography across all cohort A participants (referee 1, point 3).\n\nfig_topography.py shows one participant and the paper calls it descriptive\nevidence alongside the ICA control. The referee asked for a group-level map or\nthe consistency of the pattern across participants. This computes, for every\nparticipant on fitting sessions 1-3 exactly as fig_topography.py does:\n\n  gain  per-channel gain of M^-1/2, M built by TangentBranch.freeze_reference\n  diff  absolute 8-30 Hz power, Walk minus Stop, in dB\n\nand reports three measures of consistency:\n\n  sign agreement   per channel, how many of the 7 participants share the sign\n                   of the group mean contrast\n  sign-flip test   per channel, the group mean contrast against all 2^7 sign\n                   flips of the participants, max-statistic over channels, so\n                   the channel-wise p values are corrected across the montage\n  spatial r        mean pairwise Pearson correlation between participants' maps,\n                   against a null that shuffles channels within each map\n\nWrites results/revision/fig_topography_group.{pdf,png} and\nresults/revision/topography_group.json.\n",
